-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334924" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen