on-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334533" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334533" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "adding ${e}^{At}x(0)$ to both sides"] ["text" "differentiating and using the sum rule"] ["text" "evaluating at $t=0$"] ["text" "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-334533" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$ from ${t}_{0}$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by $\\text{integrating both sides from }{t}_{0}\\text{ to }t.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ at $t={t}_{0}$ gives\n\n$$\ny({t}_{0})={e}^{-A({t}_{0}-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})=Ix({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c8d8d435b17227597355f6ebafc08f3c666c226dbf350ecb3314d07fa60afee"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "applying a change of variables"] ["text" "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$"] ["text" "integrating both sides from ${t}_{0}$ to $t$"] ["text" "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "integrating both sides from ${t}_{0}$ to $t$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "differentiating and using the sum rule"] ["text" "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$"] ["text" "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$"] ["text" "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "differentiating and using the sum rule"] ["text" "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$"] ["text" "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$"] ["text" "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "q-335424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/state.json" "file_sha256" "266e1c2262882db8a662cce89bb25bcd04c423b6a521202c3408d2435f282ff6"} {"question" "e-21722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/101a0c499e4eb8557917785388737fb12c85713d204efaad74b13720d53d90a9.png)\nFill in the blanks in the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/b1b5a17a8facd73638545861a9ec05ee2fdebdc2ae8f327fc86f1517085bcd77.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/52808e8499c76638f512feb7dd3721814844cbfb29deb7126ed9e8872a699031.png)*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\, \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/example-21722.json" "file_sha256" "c994c6b9d2ffd483604c7566445c7fc88f2ff0eb7a1ac652d9295bd6e675e61e"} {"question" "e-21722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/ed2abaaded6d82b6ab9ae856b8f31f99d97bd34515715e36b71d2731049e5e75.png) So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/56f10da4c0759fd5616557c00ce5aa1062190b3fbaaa2ab0dff0d50ef3fb2615.png)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/example-21722.json" "file_sha256" "c994c6b9d2ffd483604c7566445c7fc88f2ff0eb7a1ac652d9295bd6e675e61e"} {"question" "e-21720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/cf38da5e2aec9fc3957f52abc58fc396686db632561953991a3ca0fc23799ace.png)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/1a1e4510a1ea4961976e22504d6be845edffd972cc88dda0fde4608b50be2b09.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/cfc60391cfb7369d109e7d56b89b6bfd1f97e7251aacb637f61c94d24cdb4f00.png)*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/example-21720.json" "file_sha256" "ab031045b0ddeaf7d393e2a24978d8028b620a4e4b171589b1f4cfa6dbb2a7f0"} {"question" "e-21720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/802292289f84a7d69cfaadd91d88d6a4af9560f618dfae6b553fbca16b63cb96.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/a851d7868235cdaf8cd6914d21b648b3bd7453549748f4bacc3caf5485c17e50.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/696a10263a0fe8a52e0da4a413956bb4040220de2c22ae41f76032f7045a5265.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/c62e0b111e20b925570d7f178ac556293597b071d9aefb821adc70d83afcb91e.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/b7b3cf84162533f6b86e3faf8bba17b335ade35acb42d18aa768a5a1db900730.png)\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t = t_0 = 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/5f80485e8a40e46b5c11656dae755f51f7b0617cbe8b4369cf330f329d042283.png)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/dbce2a7dd9077db8a6e4f85a0b54c9d2563cad3a0ef5a0a98606ca7a4bb5f81f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/example-21720.json" "file_sha256" "ab031045b0ddeaf7d393e2a24978d8028b620a4e4b171589b1f4cfa6dbb2a7f0"} {"question" "e-21721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the inhomogeneous system  $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0) = \\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\nFill in the blanks with the correct reasons to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/befe715ac2d9375061b1a3c8c0528a0bfb2764197cee4eca4d2b60146cec20b6.png).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/09febb48bb00d22caebf088103181b5db6377befccad18f1370718351cc91e9d.png).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/999db06dcfe0878ddb3316b11546668ba9442d8fd110165e5076b90964b84905.png)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/example-21721.json" "file_sha256" "21d08aff7286d7f9296eff1b1379d984f90d46cb63d9c4aa725b5d2d6047bdfd"} {"question" "e-21721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L2}$ and $\\textrm{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\textrm{L2}$ and substituting $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/9dcfd90e4444195ee781ab388b36a575ec1219d1820f7141114e29311941ddc5.png)\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Evaluating $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$ at $t=t_0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=I\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$  by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/90a07cffb30b2ef860b0d3314865a7bd9ca0b7c86811a63b07628c768188af3e.png)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\textrm{L1}$ by $e^{A(t-t_0)}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/23a2ac9e75c9bac22187814f524d919166d3748f1caa5831d664231a80bac296.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/example-21721.json" "file_sha256" "21d08aff7286d7f9296eff1b1379d984f90d46cb63d9c4aa725b5d2d6047bdfd"}] "usage" {"e-21721" [] "q-334533" [] "q-334531" [] "e-21720" [] "e-21722" []} "basis" 2538 "retractions" [[17592186229616 :question/problem "${x^{′}(t) = 2y(t); y^{′}(t) =-2x(t) + 1,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: $e^{At} = \\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (2t) & \\sin (2t) \\\\ -\\sin (2t) & \\cos (2t)\\end{bmatrix}$, where $A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix} = \\frac{1}{2}$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | $3\\sin (2t)$ |  |  |"] [17592186229617 :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system $x^{′}(t) = Ax(t) + g(t)$, where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n> $L1$: Let $y(t) = e^{-At}x(t)$\n> $L2$: $y^{′}(t) =-Ae^{-At}x(t) + e^{-At}x^{′}(t)$\n> $L3$: $y^{′}(t) = e^{-At}g(t)$\n> $L4$: $y(t) - y(0) = ∫_{0}^{t}e^{-As}g(s)ds$\n> $L5$: $y(0) = x(0)$\n> $L6$: $y(t) = x(0) + ∫_{0}^{t}e^{-As}g(s)ds$\n> $L7$: $e^{At}y(t) = e^{At}x(0) + ∫_{0}^{t}e^{A(t - s)}g(s)ds$\n> $L8$: $e^{At}y(t) = x(t)$\n> $L9$: $x(t) = e^{At}x(0) + ∫_{0}^{t}e^{A(t - s)}g(s)ds$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\nLine $L2$ follows from $L1$ by\n{{field-1}}.\n\nLine $L4$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to\n{{field-3}}.\n\nLine $L7$ follows from line $L6$ by\n{{field-4}}."] [17592186229617 :question/answer-fields 17592186228146] [17592186228868 :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nFill in the blanks in the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: $\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4t} & te^{4t} \\\\ 0 & e^{4t}\\end{bmatrix}$ where $\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$*\n\n$x(t)|= \\begin{bmatrix}X X X X \\\\ 3e^{4(t - 1)}\\end{bmatrix} + ∫_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4t} \\\\ X X\\end{bmatrix}ds$."] [17592186228868 :question/worked-solution "Given the system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that $\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4t} & te^{4t} \\\\ 0 & e^{4t}\\end{bmatrix}$ So,\n$e^{A(t - 1)}x(1)|= \\begin{bmatrix}e^{4(t - 1)} & (t - 1)e^{4(t - 1)} \\\\ 0 & e^{4(t - 1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}3(t - 1)e^{4(t - 1)} \\\\ 3e^{4(t - 1)}\\end{bmatrix}$.\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4(t - s)} & (t - s)e^{4(t - s)} \\\\ 0 & e^{4(t - s)}\\end{bmatrix}$\nSo, we have\n$e^{A(t - s)}g(s)|= \\begin{bmatrix}e^{4(t - s)} & (t - s)e^{4(t - s)} \\\\ 0 & e^{4(t - s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}e^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t) &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 (t - 1) e 4 (t - 1) \\\\ 3e^{4(t - 1)}\\end{bmatrix} + ∫_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}ds\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186228866 :question/problem "${x^{′}(t) = 3x(t) + y(t) + 1; y^{′}(t) = 3y(t)$,\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: $\\begin{bmatrix}e^{3t} & te^{3t} \\\\ 0 & e^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}$ where $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$*"] [17592186228866 :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nwhere $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ So, the matrix of the system is $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nGiven the system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}e^{3t} & te^{3t} \\\\ 0 & e^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}$\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t = t_0 = 0$, we have\n$e^{A(t - t_{0})}x(0)|= e^{At}x(0); = \\begin{bmatrix}e^{3t} & te^{3t} \\\\ 0 & e^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}e^{3(t - s)} & (t - s)e^{3(t - s)} \\\\ 0 & e^{3(t - s)}\\end{bmatrix}$\nSo, we have\n$e^{A(t - s)}g(s)|= \\begin{bmatrix}e^{3(t - s)} & (t - s)e^{3(t - s)} \\\\ 0 & e^{3(t - s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}e^{3(t - s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}e^{-3s + 3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\nThus, we obtain\n$∫_{0}^{t}e^{A(t - s)}g(s)ds|= ∫_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}e^{-3s + 3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}ds; = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3}e^{-3s + 3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}_{s = 0}^{s = t}; = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}e^{3t} - \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t) &= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}e^{3t} - \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}e^{3t} - \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}e^{3t} - 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186228867 :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)$, where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below.\n\n> $\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$\n> $\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)$\n> $\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(t)$\n> $\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0) = \\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n> $\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$\n> $\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n> $\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n> $\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t)$\n> $\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\nFill in the blanks with the correct reasons to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by $AAAAAAAAAAAAAAA$.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by $AAAAAAAAAAAAAAA$.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by $AAAAAAAAAAAAAAA$."] [17592186228867 :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L2}$ and $\\textrm{L3}$. Starting from\n$\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)$\nin $\\textrm{L2}$ and substituting $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)$ from the original system gives\n$y^{′}(t)|=-Ae^{-A(t - t_{0})}x(t) + e^{-A(t - t_{0})}(Ax(t) + g(t)); =-Ae^{-A(t - t_{0})}x(t) + Ae^{-A(t - t_{0})}x(t) + e^{-A(t - t_{0})}g(t); = e^{-A(t - t_{0})}g(t)$.\nThus, $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by $x^{′}(t) = Ax(t) + g(t)$\n- Next, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L5}$. Evaluating $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$ at $t=t_0$ gives\n$\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=I\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$.\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by $t = t_{0}$\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L8}$. Multiplying both sides of\n$\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$\nfrom $\\textrm{L1}$ by $e^{A(t-t_0)}$ gives\n$e^{A(t - t_{0})}y(t)|= e^{A(t - t_{0})}e^{-A(t - t_{0})}x(t); = x(t)$.\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from $\\textrm{L1}$ by $e^{A(t - t_{0})}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186228137 17592186228138 17592186228139 17592186228140 17592186228142 17592186228143 175921